### Impact and severity

Affected: Telegram users answering multi-question `ask_user` prompts by text, and any channel whose `onAbandoned` aborts or requeues the turn. Severity: the user gets no sign that the answer was rejected. The rejected text comes back merged into their next answer, which is itself delayed by the retry backoff (7 to 33 s measured). Frequency: every incomplete reply in these runs (14 of 14). Consequence: the agent receives a stale line mixed into the next answer; with positional parsing, that can bind answers to the wrong questions.

### Additional information

Suggested fix: in the `QUESTION_INVALID_ANSWER` branch, settle the source as a terminal decision before returning the notice, as `refuseCollaborativeSteering` does for its refusal notice in `src/auto-reply/reply/queue/lifecycle.ts` ("Abandonment reopens ingress for replay; this input has a terminal policy decision"). That is, `admitFollowupRunLifecycle(followupRun)` and then `completeFollowupRunLifecycle(followupRun, "consumed")`, so `finish(true)` finds custody completed. Leaving the input unconsumed instead would be wrong: with `keepOrderOnDecline` the source would stay queued and later run as an ordinary prompt. The `QuestionDispatchRefusedError` branch ("The answer was not sent") returns its notice the same way and probably has the same problem; not tested.

Not established: which of the two callers reached `finishReplyOperationAbortedDispatch`, and behavior on api.telegram.org.

Related: #146646 (added the notice), #173760 (its wording), #190513 (numbered replies; its qa-lab scenario uses `chat.send`), #193158 (the retry failures), #189410 (abandonment and retry exhaustion; a different problem).

