## What Problem This Solves

`skills list` discovers a skill with metadata key `Café`, but `skills info` cannot inspect it using the equivalent `Cafe\u0301` spelling. The reverse normalization direction fails too.

## User Impact

Equivalent Unicode spellings resolve the same installed skill. Exact names and metadata keys retain precedence; a tie at the strongest matching tier still refuses to choose by discovery order. This is a read-only lookup fix, not a new skill naming scheme.

## Why This Change Was Made

Normalize only the existing case-insensitive comparison tier to NFC. Both the CLI exit-status decision and detail formatting already consume this shared owner. The existing separator fallback remains unchanged. Metadata keys already accept nonempty Unicode strings; canonical skill names in the native fixture stay valid ASCII. This follows the comparison-only normalization used in #190546 without changing persisted keys or adding a library.

No new configuration/default, protocol, permission, schema, dependency or migration. No generated changelog change.

