## What Problem This Solves

Session-only readers should refresh the specific Actions query that was approved. The original PR already limits delegation to `github.actions.runs` and explicitly granted repositories, but readers can manually vary supported queries within those repositories using the agent's credentials.

## User Impact

Saved summaries should use the existing `session:report` mechanism. Live widgets declare named queries fixing repository, workflow, branch, status/date filters, result limit, pull-request handling, and response fields. Session-only readers send exactly `{ ticket, queryName }`; the Gateway resolves the stored definition and rejects selectors, overrides, and flexible fallback calls. Repository-only grants do not implicitly authorize named queries.

Approval deliberately shares selected private and future matching results obtained with the agent's GitHub credentials. Every semantic definition edit, including narrowing, renews approval under the existing Full/Auto/Ask policy. Existing repository-only HTML widgets need an approved named query for session-only live refresh; they are not converted automatically. General Gateway readers retain their existing flexible API and repository-grant contract.

## Implementation

This uses the existing widget declaration, grant store, approval policy, RPC, Actions adapter, and credential-scoped transport cache. It adds no permission store, table, config option, protocol version, or RPC. The protected bridge and authoring tool use `openclaw.data.query(name)`.

The Gateway preserves current session visibility, widget revision/generation, exact grant, credential, and revocation checks through final delivery, including cached/shared results. Pending and granted approval details display the complete query and its private/future-result sharing consequence, while retaining localized network/tool labels, bold group headings, and bullet lists.

This is a product/authorization-scope repair, not an assertion that the original PR necessarily violates `SECURITY.md`.

