Fixes #94597.

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes group-chat messages sent through action-only plugins being acknowledged as private replies or rejected as unavailable when the message tool infers the current destination.

## User Impact

Plugins that implement message actions independently of an outbound adapter can send to the current conversation, including Gateway-owned actions. Ordinary senders and private WebChat replies keep their existing routing. No configuration or migration is required.

## Why This Change Was Made

Carry the requested action through the existing channel selection and lazy activation owners, then use the same operation when the Gateway selects its handler. A shared capability predicate recognizes supported legacy action handlers; account, registry and live-authority checks still decide execution. Gateway action selection and canonical fallback live in the existing channel-resolution sibling.

